          "changes": [],
          "changeMeaning": "Shows the central atom and water Lewis structure to introduce VSEPR.",
          "narration": "Welcome to the VSEPR theory lab. VSEPR stands for Valence Shell Electron Pair Repulsion. Look at the central atom before you. Electrons in bonding pairs and lone pairs repel each other. The molecule adopts a 3D geometry that places these electron domains as far apart as possible. The Lewis structure of water on the right shows us four total electron domains around oxygen."
        }
